{"labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}, {"id": 1, "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "enpe7n7le01ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe7n7le01ob11re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "enpe7n7le01ob11re2img01.jpg", "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Steve: </strong>  What am I supposed to do? I can't understand ISM!<br>\n<strong>Mike: </strong>  Calm down! Listen to me. An information system model has four elements: customers, business processes, product services, and communication technology. These four elements are the cornerstone of competitiveness today. An edge can be achieved by a company implementing better information systems that bring help in processing information more effectively and efficiently than other rivals. </br> When technology is inserted in a company, both the company's internal communication (email, chat, etc.) and external communication (websites, and tools like webinar, etc.) can be improved. Thus, the internal data processing for manufacturing, logistics, or finance operations, as well as the channel of communication with the company's customers can be assessed as being more effective. Unquestionably, not only sales but also the solutions offered to customers on their requests show improvement when companies decide to put technology to use.<br>That's why implementing information systems is so important.", "time": "0"}, {"id": 1, "image": "enpe7n7le01ob11re2img02.jpg", "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Steve: </strong>  I see, but how can customer and product services be considered an advantage for a company? How are they supposed to help a company? <br>\n<strong>Mike: </strong>  An effective ISM is supposed to be designed and developed to meet the needs and expectations of both internal and external clients. This means that data processing should go through different processes before reaching an ending result that is beneficial for internal and external clients. For example, think of a bank that offers internet banking. All banking tasks can be completed by a customer without visiting the bank. This can be considered an effective product service in ISM. <br>", "time": "75000"}, {"id": 2, "image": "enpe7n7le01ob11re2img03.jpg", "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Steve: </strong>  What about the other two elements? <br>\n<strong>Mike: </strong> A business has many different processes which can be streamlined by adding, changing, or eliminating some steps. Information is key in doing these tasks. More cost-efficient processes mean profits to a business. Of course, all of this can be achieved by taking advantage of new technologies and communication technologies. Are they supposed to bring any benefits? The answer is yes. In fact, we are evidencing that with the inclusion of new technological apps, chats, and dynamic websites.<br>", "time": "117500"}]}}], "_data": []}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about the importance of some elements in the design of an information system model.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can discuss information about customers, products and services in the design of an information system model.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can exchange ideas about business processes and communication technology.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What models can be created to solve information problems at work or college?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " In your opinion, what are the benefits of using communication technologies at work?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedba