"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Elements of Information System Model ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about the elements of an Information System Model.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand information about relational database management system in spoken or written texts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses information a wider range of contexts about exchanging technical information on software programming and software solutions, using appropriate grammar and vocabulary at this level.  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on software programming, software solutions and database management.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_6"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n7le01ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Be Supposed to in Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p><strong>Be supposed</strong> to can be used in a question structure as well as in a sentence structure, either affirmative or negative.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "How are they supposed to help a company? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Are they supposed to bring any benefits? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What am I supposed to do?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<p>The meaning of <strong>be supposed to</strong> in a question depends on the context the question is used. The contexts are those explained above.</p> <p>Grammatical structure:</p> <p>You can use be supposed to for both <strong>wh- questions</strong> and <strong>yes/no</strong>. Take a look at the examples below:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Wh + Be + subject + supposed to + verb + complement?</strong></p> <p><i>What&nbsp;<strong>are we supposed to do</strong>&nbsp;about analytics?</i></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Be + subject + supposed to + verb + complement?</strong></p> <p><i>Are we&nbsp;<strong>supposed to do</strong>&nbsp;any analysis with this financial data?</i></p> <p>As you can recognize from the two examples above, the verb <strong>be</strong> is conjugated depending on the subject it goes with. Another interesting aspect is that you can use the expression <strong>be supposed to</strong> in present and past tenses. In such cases, the verb <strong>be</strong> changes accordingly. Please, take a look at some other examples:</p> <p><i>What&nbsp;<strong>was</strong>&nbsp;Taylor&nbsp;<strong>supposed to do</strong>&nbsp;with the backup information from Farrels Inc. yesterday?</i></p> <p><i>Mike, what&nbsp;<strong>is&nbsp;</strong>this new device&nbsp;<strong>supposed to be&nbsp;</strong>used for<strong>?</strong></i></p> <p><strong>Meaning:</strong></p> <p>Now I'd like you to be aware of the meanings the expression <strong>be supposed to</strong> has in the following three questions. Look at the chart.</p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Meaning (Context)</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Question example</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's believed, said\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>I think I've seen this device earlier. What is <strong>it supposed to </strong>be used for?</i>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's planned, expected\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>I've got a question, what time am <strong>I supposed to</strong> come to the office tomorrow morning?</i>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's NOT advisable, allowed\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Mike tell me. What part of the process <strong>aren't you supposed to</strong> have access and why?</i>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Passive of Modal Verb Can", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>The <strong>modal verbs can</strong> and <strong>could</strong> combined in a <strong>passive voice form</strong> are used to express present and past ability or possibility when we are NOT interested in stating who does something, but what is done.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "All banking tasks can be completed by a customer without visiting the bank. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I see, but how can customer and product services be considered an advantage for a company?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This can be considered an effective product service in ISM.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<p>Remember that we use <strong>passive</strong> constructions to refer to something that happened without mentioning who did it. The speaker or writer decides it is not necessary to give information about the doer of the action. In relation to the use of the modals <strong>can</strong> and <strong>could</strong>, they express <strong>ability</strong> or <strong>possibility</strong>.</p> <p>To make a construction using the modal verbs <strong>can</strong>/<strong>could</strong> in <strong>passive</strong> <strong>voice</strong>, use the following formula:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Subject + can/could + be + past participle verb + complement</strong></p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><i>Loss of data&nbsp;<strong>could be produced</strong>&nbsp;due to a hacker attack.</i></p> <p><i>An information system&nbsp;<strong>can be improved</strong>&nbsp;if end user requests are carefully considered.</i></p> <p>Affirmative and negative forms are used, too. To use the negative form simply add the word NOT after the modal verb.</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Subject + can NOT /could NOT + be + past participle verb + complement</strong></p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><i>Loss of data&nbsp;<strong>could not be caused</strong>&nbsp;by internal data mismanagement.</i></p> <p><i>An information system&nbsp;<strong>cannot be improved</strong>&nbsp;if end user requests are carelessly considered.</i></p>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "edge ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "advantage", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: An edge can be achieved by a company implementing better information systems.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n7le01ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rival ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person, group, company, etc., competing against others  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: An edge can be achieved by a company implementing better information systems that bring help in processing information more effectively and efficiently than other rivals. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n7le01ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "data processing ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the conversion of raw input data for the purpose of storing, transforming, rearranging, and updating ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The internal data processing for manufacturing, logistics, or finance operations, as well as the channel of communication with the company's customers can be assessed as being more effective. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n7le01ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "banking tasks ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "activities related to money management, money collection and money deposits ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: All banking tasks can be completed by a customer without visiting the bank.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n7le01ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "streamline ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to improve the effectiveness of a process, organization or business ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A business has many different processes which can be streamlined by adding, changing, or eliminating some steps.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n7le01ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "competitiveness ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the ability of a person or organization to compete and achieve the results wanted or hoped for", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: These four elements are the cornerstone of competitiveness today. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n7le01ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Search for more characteristics of customers, business processes, communication, products and services.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a paragraph explaining why they are so important in the design of an information system model. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your paragraph with a partner. Read it aloud. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I search for information about characteristics of customers, business processes, communication, products and services. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a paragraph explaining why they are so important in the design of an information system model. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my paragraph and read it aloud. ", "type": "text"}]}]}